      detail: `Checklist: Each integration has one entry in config/integrations.json, one Logic App and one managed identity, and lists every workflow it serves. lcwext.py lint reports no findings against the entry's timeoutDuration, and build produced the deployed ARM resource and extension. The extension uses proof-of-possession, launch and wait, and the Logic App's identity as its only authorized app. The Logic App has SAS turned off and Learn's PoP policy, with the appid confirmed in the tenant. graphHost matches the tenant's cloud; GCC uses graph.microsoft.com. The downstream system honors Idempotency-Key, and a repeat delivery was tested. A forced downstream failure produced a failed callback within minutes in the test tenant. In every leaver workflow, Disable user account and Revoke all refresh tokens for user run before the custom task. The managed identity has no tenant-wide Lifecycle Workflows permission. The pinned Learn page matches its manifest, and every upstream commit since the pin has been reviewed. Next: Chapter 06 — Moving Group Policy as Code.`,
